{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003954-101-acts-of-hubris-examples-for-dummies","id":1003954,"title":"101 Acts Of Hubris - Examples for Dummies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T08:31:02-08:00","id":1003954,"title":"101 Acts Of Hubris - Examples for Dummies","content":"Once again I'm making a thread about Hubris and It's again because I'm not firm in choosing what can be an Act. So I've come to bargain.<br /> Can you give some examples of when you rolled for Hubris in your games? Here are mine.<ul><li>Harming your cabalmates with badly aimed spell</li> <li>Beliving in your abilities too much and entering unknown realm by means of Space magic only to realize that this one Exceptional Success you had on piercing through won't be easy to replicate. And you are stuck without mage armor facing immediate danger.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-17-2016, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:38:25-08:00","id":1003956,"title":"","content":"My character believes that &quot;good luck&quot; you get from her Fate spells has to come from somewhere. Basically, if I give myself good luck, someone else, somewhere, is getting bad luck. &quot;Karma balance&quot;. This leads to her doing Hubris rolls whenever she casts Fate spells that might have too much unseen impact on other people; she will never see what *could* or *did* happen to people that had to be manipulated by magic to make sure that, I don't know, YOUR Pizza order will arrive in time, so she assumes the worst. <br /> <br /> Other, fairly innocent one, was using Death to make hot weather bearable and not make her smelly due to wearing her full Shadow Name related attire in full summer sun. This one was because one of her major fears is being so disconnected from normal human experience that she might stop being qualified to being human, and one of human-defining things is facing hardships. Even little ones like these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T02:16:23-08:00","id":1004304,"title":"","content":"Those are so great WHW! I'm really looking forward to seeing more examples from your cabal.<br /> Also I would love to see some examples from the rest of the forum frequenters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The more the better but one or two is already a lot for me and, I hope, for a few others here who are not so confident in judging Hubris yet.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://ih1.redbubble.net/image.23982342.6514/raf,750x1000,075,t,heather_grey.2u11.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-17-2016, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T02:39:13-08:00","id":1004309,"title":"","content":"My ST wanted me to roll for an act of hubris, but he felt he had to label the act as a sin against enlightened wisdom (8 or higher) and my character only had a 7 (typical starting level). He had created these automatons that had an aspect of life and intelligence to them. My character wanted to find out exactly how intelligent they were, so he cast an unveiling of mind spell at them. Since they were built with defenses against mind spells and he couldn't break them the first time, he cast it again and again. The other players wanted to know why, and when the ST said that the leader automaton asked my character a question (specifically &quot;What is it that you want to know?), I said ooc that my character didn't WANT to talk to the machines (after all, you can't exactly just ask someone/something how intelligent they/it are/is). They couldn't believe it. However, since the spell wasn't intrusive, he labeled it a sin against enlightened wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T03:39:00-08:00","id":1004321,"title":"","content":"Actually, none of the examples here would be considered Acts of Hubris in my group. Always good to see these threads and get a different perspective <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We've considered it as an Act against Understanding Wisdom that time our Obrimos used Mind to get a free hotel room, when he had enough money to pay for it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T04:28:57-08:00","id":1004330,"title":"","content":"I have a player who was trying to avoid some cops and ended up reversing the local gravity under their car. He didn't lift them far, about ten feet, but, yeah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:54:34-08:00","id":1004423,"title":"","content":"A ten foot drop is still sufficient to kill you if you hit your head on something.<br /> <br /> It is surprisingly easy <i>and</i> difficult to kill a human being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003954-101-acts-of-hubris-examples-for-dummies?p=1004309#post1004309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ST wanted me to roll for an act of hubris, but he felt he had to label the act as a sin against enlightened wisdom (8 or higher) and my character only had a 7 (typical starting level). He had created these automatons that had an aspect of life and intelligence to them. My character wanted to find out exactly how intelligent they were, so he cast an unveiling of mind spell at them. Since they were built with defenses against mind spells and he couldn't break them the first time, he cast it again and again. The other players wanted to know why, and when the ST said that the leader automaton asked my character a question (specifically &quot;What is it that you want to know?), I said ooc that my character didn't WANT to talk to the machines (after all, you can't exactly just ask someone/something how intelligent they/it are/is). They couldn't believe it. However, since the spell wasn't intrusive, he labeled it a sin against enlightened wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually pretty incredible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T03:47:47-08:00","id":1004864,"title":"","content":"Love those. Still, the more the better so if you have some you know what to do. A quick question to be sure: Killing someone with absolutely no usage of magic is not a AoH no matter how gruesome or unnecessary it is, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T03:52:33-08:00","id":1004865,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm pretty sure that Dave has said that mundane actions could be acts of hubris too. I could be wrong about that, though. I know the idea has been mentioned before and that he commented on it....I'll see if I can find the source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T03:59:06-08:00","id":1004867,"title":"","content":"Source would be great, thanks. I would rule that if it is an AoH it is tier higher then it would be with using magic. Kinda like with premeditated and rage murder. So premeditated murder with no magic would an enlightened sin and rage murder would be understanding sin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:17:28-08:00","id":1004922,"title":"","content":"Oh, my. There have been huge discussions about &quot;Does it need to be magic to be Hubris&quot; already, you can catch a spotlight of one of those threads <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887107-understand-wisdom?p=895967#post895967\">here</a> (a most wonderful rant by ArcaneArts). Please, let's not derails this thread with that discussion, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:12:56-08:00","id":1005006,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4854\" data-vbnamecard=\"4854\">Justin Sane</a> for the link, worth of reading. How could I missed that thread? Anyway, any spare examples of Hubris for an old poor beggar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:51:01-08:00","id":1005117,"title":"","content":"It's very important to ask yourself a question before you proceed: what function do you want your Acts of Hubris to fulfill? There are few options here, and having both you and your players on the same page helps very much. It also would greatly increase value of any examples given to include &quot;why is this an act of hubris in our game&quot; and &quot;what purpose did it serve to roll for hubris at that time&quot;, from meta point of view.<br /> <br /> My first two examples came from a point of view that in out game, Hubris should be another way to tell everyone something about our characters. As you can see, &quot;camera&quot; and &quot;focus&quot; in my examples was directed towards &quot;why&quot; and &quot;what is my relationship with magic&quot;. Character X would not roll for Hubris using these same spells in the same situation, but because of very specific personality of my character and her attitude towards magic, it was feeling right to do so. Note, our AoHs are very pretty much self inflicted and self-called.<br /> So, our Hubris:<br /> 1. Serves as a NARRATIVE DEVICE, a tool to flesh out characters and introduce new information about them, put old info in context, and in general, &quot;let you know them better&quot;.<br /> 2. Serves as a METAGAME TOOL used to push game into more genre-fitting direction; it's a carrot for creating problems in exchange for Beats.<br /> <br /> However, in other games, Hubris can be a way to discourage and deter from certain acts and gameplay style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:02:08-08:00","id":1005394,"title":"","content":"I've read the previous threads and came to better understand hubris, thanks! The question is why is it so harsh? 3 dice on average roll. Pre errat\u0105 version allowed adding wilower but now you are stuck with a coin flip.<br /> And you can regain one dot of wisdom per story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> Its not a carrot anymore after errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-19-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:15:02-08:00","id":1005400,"title":"","content":"3 dice is still ~65% odds of success. If you could spend Willpower and roll 6 dice, the odds of failure would be tiny, and unless you're a total maniac (in which case your Wisdom <i>ought</i> to be cratering) you're going to have a lot more Willpower than Hubris rolls, so if you <i>could</i> add it, you would basically always do so. Not allowing Willpower expenditure on it makes the roll matter, because failure is a realistic possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:26:49-08:00","id":1005403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003954-101-acts-of-hubris-examples-for-dummies?p=1005394#post1005394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read the previous threads and came to better understand hubris, thanks! The question is why is it so harsh? 3 dice on average roll. Pre errat\u0105 version allowed adding wilower but now you are stuck with a coin flip.<br /> And you can regain one dot of wisdom per story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> Its not a carrot anymore after errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post-errata: Any time your character risks Wisdom degeneration, she<br /> gains an Arcane Beat. Exploring the depths of hubris can be<br /> enlightening.<br /> <br /> So yes, it's still a carrot. Also note, that's just whenever you risk it, you don't have to drop in Wisdom to get that Beat. So it's a hell of a good carrot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:41:45-08:00","id":1005406,"title":"","content":"Just don't call it a carrot.. After 8 rolls of AoH you end up with 1xp and 3 beats.In the meantime your wisdom will drop by 2 or more - it's worth 4xp. That's kind of ok but don't call it a carrot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:29:49-08:00","id":1005412,"title":"","content":"It's an incentive and those are typically known as carrots around here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:58:59-08:00","id":1005424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003954-101-acts-of-hubris-examples-for-dummies?p=1005394#post1005394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read the previous threads and came to better understand hubris, thanks! The question is why is it so harsh? 3 dice on average roll. Pre errat\u0105 version allowed adding wilower but now you are stuck with a coin flip.<br /> And you can regain one dot of wisdom per story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> Its not a carrot anymore after errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had a conversation about this in one of past threads, and Dave pitched in that you can and should spend Willpower on Wisdom if you want to keep it high. I don't remember it being changed in the errata, but I can't refer to books right now, and I usually rely on my own all-i-need cheatsheet :P. Note that for High Wisdom character, constantly challenging their Wisdom is both fun and profitable, as High Wisdom Hubris has naturally good dicepool, and Willpowering it makes failure really tiny. <br /> <br /> By the way, there are some &quot;variables&quot; you should think about to make the most out of your Hubris:<br /> <br /> 1. What goal I want to achieve by using Act of Hubris mechanic? Do I want to make it a carrot? Do I want to make it a tool to flesh out characters more? Do I want use it to discourage certain behaviors? Do I want to use it to encourage certain behaviors? Do i want to use it to &quot;model&quot; certain style of magic society? <br /> <br /> After thinking about it really hard, you should think about, having your goal still in mind:<br /> <br /> 2. How often do I want AoH to trigger? Any time they are applicable? About once per scene? Once per chapter?<br /> <br /> 3. WHEN do I want AoH to be rolled? In the same combat turn? At the end of the scene? At end of the game session? At start of the game session?<br /> <br /> 4. Is there any houserule that would make working towards my goal smoother? For example, if I want it to be a carrot, I might consider removing XP for regaining Wisdom and make it free for resolving WIsdom-redemption Obsession instead; I might disallow or allow Willpower expenditure depending on how often I want characters to actually drop Wisdom; I might make mundane acts count or not count as Hubris depending on what angle I want to tangle.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Acts of Hubris are a fascinating mechanic to write about and you could talk all day about how to use them in a way that will maximize enjoyment of your experience. I don't have much time lately, but &quot;Do It Your Own Hubris&quot; thread with a step by step guideline what can be hacked and modded in Wisdom rules would be something very interesting to write and read.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:41:04-08:00","id":1005812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003954-101-acts-of-hubris-examples-for-dummies?p=1005424#post1005424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We had a conversation about this in one of past threads, and Dave pitched in that you can and should spend Willpower on Wisdom if you want to keep it high. </div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly mentioned in the section that you can't use willpower on the roll in the final version of the book. It surprised me as well after seeing that discussion. It's not listed in the official errata that was put out after the advanced copy feedback was given but it is in the final copy of the book. Does anyone know if this is a change for CoD Integrity as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7892-malraza","name":"Malraza","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:44:46-08:00","id":1006120,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> when you wrote your post I've already been tweaking the rules for my chronicle. Wisdom dot costs one a.xp but beats must come from specific obsession pertaining the wisdom recovery. You can use willpower on a roll but it is worth only +1 like any other modification for this roll. <br /> <br /> <br /> And I would love to see a chapter about telling a story with Hubris mechanics with examples, tweaks and alternate mechanics - sadly its a thing for a Storyteller's Guide book. But I would read the shit out of it if you you write your take on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}